>>> I hear a lot of different opinions. Some like the experiment, some loathe
>>> it.
>>
>> As a newbie, I like the experiment.  I bet the "normal" look will do
>> wonders for lojban popularity.  Right now, lojban looks like a specialized
>> language for some bizarre, obscure purpose such as defining ontologies for
>> Prolog or Lisp expert systems.  And who besides purists could use it in
>> that form?  But after your style is finalized, lojban should finally be
>> recognizable as a real tongue, useful for ordinary human-to-human
>> interaction.  Besides, beautiful typography never hurts book sales.
>
> I hope that there is a balance that can be struck.
